{"id":"4431452","name":"Drake Maye","team":"NE","pos":"QB","grp":"QB","num":"10","head":"https://a.espncdn.com/i/headshots/nfl/players/full/4431452.png","age":24,"exp":"3","college":"North Carolina","draft":["2024","1","3"],"depth":{"pos":"QB","rank":3,"unit":"3WR 1TE","team":"NE"},"inj":{"current":true,"status":"Out","note":"Per Reiss, teams are limited to eight players that can be designated to return from the list over the course of the regular season, and the Patriots are close to using them all. \"Right now, he's not on injured reserve,\" Vrabel said Monday. \"He's on the active roster, so that's where it is today. I think that those things are obviously fluid. But we want to try to give him every opportunity that we can to be back at some point in time. I don't know when that will be; I'm not sure. But also, try to manage the roster and do what we need to do to try to win each week.\" On Sunday, reporters reported that Maye was on track to miss at least six weeks, a timetable that suggests, in a best-case scenario, the QB could make a push for a late-season return or for the postseason, should New England qualify. Heading into a Week 12 game against the Chargers, Tommy DeVito is slated to work as the team's starter, with rookie Behren Morton on hand as his backup. Additionally, there's the possibility that the team considers Daniel Jones -- who the Colts let go Friday -- as an alternative, but Vrabel told Reiss that in the short term at least, adding another signal-caller is not something that's being planned.","date":"2026-11-23T20:26:00.000+00:00","detail":"Lower Leg","reserve":false,"ret":"2026-12-27T00:00:00.000+00:00"},"next":{"opp":"LAC","home":false,"date":"2026-11-29T21:05Z"},"dvp":{"r":18,"td":1.8,"yds":245.4,"n":32,"g":10},"news":[{"h":"Patriots-Chargers shaping up to be battle of backup QBs for 2 of AFC's biggest disappointments","d":"\u2014 When Drake Maye\u2019s New England Patriots eased past Justin Herbert\u2019s Los Angeles Chargers in an AFC w